# GraphRAG private IP — vocab / templates / params / gold sets / corpus profile.
# (The schema CODE under src/leviathan/graphrag/ is public; only these configs are private.)
#
# THE SHIPPED SUBJECT-RESOLVER DECKS ARE THE ONE STATED EXCEPTION, and it is written here rather than
# carried by an invisible `git add -f`. D9 of the subject-resolver sitting requires the calibration
# deck to be FORCE-TRACKED like `driver_slices.yaml`; v1 and v2 are in the repository on exactly that
# ruling, but on a rule nobody could read -- so v3 was authored, pinned by four tests, and left
# OUTSIDE the repository, where a commit by explicit path refuses the path and lands a red tree.
# The directory rule is therefore spelled `configs/graphrag/*` and the three decks are named back in:
# a TRAILING-SLASH rule excludes the DIRECTORY itself, and git cannot re-include a file whose parent
# directory is excluded, so the negations below only work in this form. Nothing else changes -- every
# other entry under `configs/graphrag/`, subdirectories included, is ignored exactly as before.
# THE HELD-OUT DECK IS NOT HERE AND NEVER WILL BE: it lives outside the repository by design.
configs/graphrag/*
!configs/graphrag/subject_deck_v1.yaml
!configs/graphrag/subject_deck_v2.yaml
!configs/graphrag/subject_deck_v3.yaml
docs/graphrag/corpus_profile/

# Claude working files
.claude/

# Terraform
**/.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.backup
# Any suffixed state copy (.backup, .pre_batch_YYYYMMDD, terraform's own .NNNN.backup).
# `*.tfstate` does NOT match these, and the state carries the Google OAuth client secret,
# 15 Secrets Manager ARNs and the RDS endpoint. This repo is PUBLIC.
*.tfstate.*
*.tfvars
!*.tfvars.example
.terraform.lock.hcl


# Leviathan product / UI design + build plans — PRIVATE, never public
docs/private/

# terraform saved plans (may embed sensitive values) + plan text dumps
infra/terraform/**/tfplan*
infra/terraform/**/*.tfplan

# F2 pre-flight (public repo hardening): approval secrets + identity-bearing evidence artifacts
scratch/
reports/silver_readiness/

# build-time copy of configs/silver bundled into the wheel (setup.py); the tracked configs/ tree is the source of truth
src/leviathan/silver/_contract_configs/
